// The Realtime Database is not used by this project — all data lives in Firestore
// (see firestore.rules). These rules were '.read'/'.write': 'auth != null' on the
// root, so any account on this Firebase project had full control of the whole
// database. Nothing reads or writes here, so it is closed outright. If RTDB is ever
// adopted, add per-path rules rather than reopening the root.
//
// The note has to be a `//` line comment, not a `"//"` key: the rules parser accepts
// only a `rules` property at the root and rejects the file outright otherwise.
{
  "rules": {
    ".read": false,
    ".write": false
  }
}
